# The winning config from section 2 (pruning), sourced by
# pruning_2b_fi_tune_array.job (uses everything except ENET_CHANNELS' f_i,
# which it sweeps) and postpruning_3a_quant_array.job (uses everything, and
# sweeps ENET_QUANT_BITS instead) -- edited in one place as section 2
# resolves, not duplicated per job script.
#
# REAL WINNER of section 2a's grid (compression/slurm/pruning_2a_grid_array.job,
# 19 runs) -- nnUNetTrainerENet_2a_O8_native, top score in
# compression/results/ranking.csv (score -0.1912, Dice 0.7187, 7406 params,
# 234.4M FLOPs). O8 x native-bottleneck: O8 = (16,8,16,8,4) is O8's position
# on the ENET-ORIGINAL-derived filter axis (O1=Original, O2, O4, O8, O16, OF
# -- see foundation_log.md's "Plan revision 2" section), native = the
# ENet-paper bottleneck-depth pattern (4,8,8,2,1), unreduced.
#
# Update ENET_CHANNELS' f_i specifically after 2b
# (compression/slurm/pruning_2b_fi_tune_array.job, f_i in [36,12,8,4],
# reusing f_i=16 from 2a) picks the final f_i.
# ENET_DECODER_TYPE/USE_DILATED/USE_ASYMMETRIC/USE_STRIDED/USE_DSC come from
# cfinal_ops.env (1b/1c's output), not duplicated here -- both files get
# sourced together by 2b/3a.

export ENET_CHANNELS="16,8,16,8,4"
export ENET_BOTTLENECKS="4,8,8,2,1"
